---Specifies options for controlling advanced machine features.
---Options that would traditionally be configured in a BIOS belong
---here. Features that require operating system support may have
---corresponding entries in the GuestOsFeatures of anImage (e.g., whether or not the OS in theImage supports nested virtualization being enabled or
---disabled).
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AdvancedMachineFeatures
---@field performanceMonitoringUnit? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AdvancedMachineFeaturesPerformanceMonitoringUnitEnum|string Type of Performance Monitoring Unit requested on instance.
---@field enableWatchdogTimer? boolean Whether to enable the watchdog timer.
---@field numaNodeCount? number The number of vNUMA nodes.
---@field turboMode? string Turbo frequency mode to use for the instance. Supported modes include: * ALL_CORE_MAX Using empty string or not setting this field will use the platform-specific default turbo mode.
---@field enableNestedVirtualization? boolean Whether to enable nested virtualization or not (default is false).
---@field visibleCoreCount? number The number of physical cores to expose to an instance. Multiply by the number of threads per core to compute the total number of virtual CPUs to expose to the instance. If unset, the number of cores is inferred from the instance's nominal CPU count and the underlying platform's SMT width.
---@field enableUefiNetworking? boolean Whether to enable UEFI networking for instance creation.
---@field threadsPerCore? number The number of threads per physical core. To disable simultaneous multithreading (SMT) set this to 1. If unset, the maximum number of threads supported per core by the underlying processor is assumed.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AdvancedMachineFeaturesPerformanceMonitoringUnitEnum "ARCHITECTURAL"|"ENHANCED"|"PERFORMANCE_MONITORING_UNIT_UNSPECIFIED"|"STANDARD"

