---An alias IP range attached to an instance's network interface.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AliasIpRange
---@field ipCidrRange? string The IP alias ranges to allocate for this interface. This IP CIDR range must belong to the specified subnetwork and cannot contain IP addresses reserved by system or used by other network interfaces. This range may be a single IP address (such as 10.2.3.4), a netmask (such as/24) or a CIDR-formatted string (such as10.1.2.0/24).
---@field candidateSubnetworkRangeNames? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Identifies the candidate subnetwork range names for the alias IPs to be allocated from. When it is set, the IP would be allocated from any subnetwork range defined here if the IPs are available. Only one of subnetwork_range_name or candidate_subnetwork_range_names should be set.
---@field subnetworkRangeName? string The name of a subnetwork secondary IP range from which to allocate an IP alias range. If not specified, the primary range of the subnetwork is used.
---@field effectiveSubnetworkRangeName? string Output only. [Output Only] The subnetwork range name where the IP is allocated. It will be set to the subnetwork range where the IP is allocated only.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AliasIpRangeList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AliasIpRange[]

---This reservation type is specified by total resource amounts (e.g. total
---count of CPUs) and can account for multiple instance SKUs. In other words,
---one can create instances of varying shapes against this reservation.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservation
---@field reservedResources? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservationReservedResourceInfoList List of reserved resources (CPUs, memory, accelerators).
---@field inUseHostCount? number Output only. Number of hosts currently in use. If there is one or more Instances running on the host, it is considered in use.
---@field vmFamily? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservationVmFamilyEnum|string The VM family that all instances scheduled against this reservation must belong to.
---@field inUseResources? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservationReservedResourceInfoList Output only. [Output only] List of resources currently in use.
---@field inUseInstanceCount? number Output only. Number of instances currently in use in this reservation.
---@field workloadType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservationWorkloadTypeEnum|string The workload type of the instances that will target this reservation.
---@field hostCount? number Count of reserved hosts of specified VM family. The host has fixed number of accelerators based on the accelerator/vm-family selected.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservationReservedResourceInfo
---@field accelerator? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservationReservedResourceInfoAccelerator Properties of accelerator resources in this reservation.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservationReservedResourceInfoAccelerator
