---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationSpecificSKUReservation
---@field inUseCount? string Output only. [Output Only] Indicates how many instances are in use.
---@field instanceProperties? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationSpecificSKUAllocationReservedInstanceProperties The instance properties for the reservation.
---@field assuredCount? string Output only. [Output Only] Indicates how many instances are actually usable currently.
---@field sourceInstanceTemplate? string Specifies the instance template to create the reservation. If you use this field, you must exclude the instanceProperties field. This field is optional, and it can be a full or partial URL. For example, the following are all valid URLs to an instance template: - https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/project/global/instanceTemplates/instanceTemplate - projects/project/global/instanceTemplates/instanceTemplate - global/instanceTemplates/instanceTemplate
---@field count? string Specifies the number of resources that are allocated.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AnnouncePublicAdvertisedPrefixesRequest
---@field project string Project ID for this request.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field publicAdvertisedPrefix string The name of the public advertised prefix. It should comply with RFC1035.

