---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ApplyUpdatesToInstancesInstanceGroupManagersRequest
---@field minimalAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestMinimalActionEnum|string The minimal action that you want to perform on each instance during the update: - REPLACE: At minimum, delete the instance and create it again. - RESTART: Stop the instance and start it again. - REFRESH: Do not stop the instance and limit disruption as much as possible. - NONE: Do not disrupt the instance at all. By default, the minimum action is NONE. If your update requires a more disruptive action than you set with this flag, the necessary action is performed to execute the update.
---@field allInstances? boolean Flag to update all instances instead of specified list of "instances". If the flag is set to true then the instances may not be specified in the request.
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList The list of URLs of one or more instances for which you want to apply updates. Each URL can be a full URL or a partial URL, such aszones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME].
---@field allowedActions? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestAllowedActionsItemEnumList Actions that are allowed to update instances within MIG.
---@field maximalAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestMaximalActionEnum|string The maximal action that should be performed on the instances. By default REPLACE. This field is deprecated, please use most_disruptive_allowed_action.
---@field mostDisruptiveAllowedAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestMostDisruptiveAllowedActionEnum|string The most disruptive action that you want to perform on each instance during the update: - REPLACE: Delete the instance and create it again. - RESTART: Stop the instance and start it again. - REFRESH: Do not stop the instance and limit disruption as much as possible. - NONE: Do not disrupt the instance at all. By default, the most disruptive allowed action is REPLACE. If your update requires a more disruptive action than you set with this flag, the update request will fail.
---@field zone string The name of thezone where the managed instance group is located. Should conform to RFC1035.
---@field instanceGroupManager string The name of the managed instance group, should conform to RFC1035.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ApplyUpdatesToInstancesRegionInstanceGroupManagersRequest
---@field allInstances? boolean Flag to update all instances instead of specified list of "instances". If the flag is set to true then the instances may not be specified in the request.
---@field minimalAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RegionInstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestMinimalActionEnum|string The minimal action that you want to perform on each instance during the update: - REPLACE: At minimum, delete the instance and create it again. - RESTART: Stop the instance and start it again. - REFRESH: Do not stop the instance and limit disruption as much as possible. - NONE: Do not disrupt the instance at all. By default, the minimum action is NONE. If your update requires a more disruptive action than you set with this flag, the necessary action is performed to execute the update.
---@field mostDisruptiveAllowedAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RegionInstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestMostDisruptiveAllowedActionEnum|string The most disruptive action that you want to perform on each instance during the update: - REPLACE: Delete the instance and create it again. - RESTART: Stop the instance and start it again. - REFRESH: Do not stop the instance and limit disruption as much as possible. - NONE: Do not disrupt the instance at all. By default, the most disruptive allowed action is REPLACE. If your update requires a more disruptive action than you set with this flag, the update request will fail.
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList The list of URLs of one or more instances for which you want to apply updates. Each URL can be a full URL or a partial URL, such aszones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME].
---@field maximalAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RegionInstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestMaximalActionEnum|string The maximal action that should be performed on the instances. By default REPLACE. This field is deprecated, please use most_disruptive_allowed_action.
---@field allowedActions? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RegionInstanceGroupManagersApplyUpdatesRequestAllowedActionsItemEnumList Actions that are allowed to update instances within MIG.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.
---@field region string Name of the region scoping this request, should conform to RFC1035.
---@field instanceGroupManager string The name of the managed instance group, should conform to RFC1035.

