---Specifies the audit configuration for a service.
---The configuration determines which permission types are logged, and what
---identities, if any, are exempted from logging.
---An AuditConfig must have one or more AuditLogConfigs.
---
---If there are AuditConfigs for both `allServices` and a specific service,
---the union of the two AuditConfigs is used for that service: the log_types
---specified in each AuditConfig are enabled, and the exempted_members in each
---AuditLogConfig are exempted.
---
---Example Policy with multiple AuditConfigs:
---
---    {
---      "audit_configs": [
---        {
---          "service": "allServices",
---          "audit_log_configs": [
---            {
---              "log_type": "DATA_READ",
---              "exempted_members": [
---                "user:jose@example.com"
---              ]
---            },
---            {
---              "log_type": "DATA_WRITE"
---            },
---            {
---              "log_type": "ADMIN_READ"
---            }
---          ]
---        },
---        {
---          "service": "sampleservice.googleapis.com",
---          "audit_log_configs": [
---            {
---              "log_type": "DATA_READ"
---            },
---            {
---              "log_type": "DATA_WRITE",
---              "exempted_members": [
---                "user:aliya@example.com"
---              ]
---            }
---          ]
---        }
---      ]
---    }
---
---For sampleservice, this policy enables DATA_READ, DATA_WRITE and ADMIN_READ
---logging. It also exempts `jose@example.com` from DATA_READ logging, and
---`aliya@example.com` from DATA_WRITE logging.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditConfig
---@field service? string Specifies a service that will be enabled for audit logging. For example, `storage.googleapis.com`, `cloudsql.googleapis.com`. `allServices` is a special value that covers all services.
---@field auditLogConfigs? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditLogConfigList The configuration for logging of each type of permission.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditConfigList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditConfig[]

---Provides the configuration for logging a type of permissions.
---Example:
---
---    {
---      "audit_log_configs": [
---        {
---          "log_type": "DATA_READ",
---          "exempted_members": [
---            "user:jose@example.com"
---          ]
---        },
---        {
---          "log_type": "DATA_WRITE"
---        }
---      ]
---    }
---
---This enables 'DATA_READ' and 'DATA_WRITE' logging, while exempting
---jose@example.com from DATA_READ logging.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditLogConfig
---@field logType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditLogConfigLogTypeEnum|string The log type that this config enables.
---@field exemptedMembers? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Specifies the identities that do not cause logging for this type of permission. Follows the same format of Binding.members.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditLogConfigList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditLogConfig[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuditLogConfigLogTypeEnum "ADMIN_READ"|"DATA_READ"|"DATA_WRITE"|"LOG_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"

---Authentication configuration for the management interface, typically using
---mTLS.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuthenticationConfig
---@field trustConfig? string Required. Resource name of the Cloud Certificate Manager TrustConfig used to validate client certificates for mTLS. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/trustConfigs/{trust_config}

---[Deprecated] The authentication settings for the backend service.
---The authentication settings for the backend service.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuthenticationPolicy
---@field serverTlsContext? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.TlsContext Configures the mechanism to obtain server-side security certificates and identity information.
---@field origins? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.OriginAuthenticationMethodList List of authentication methods that can be used for origin authentication. Similar to peers, these will be evaluated in order the first valid one will be used to set origin identity. If none of these methods pass, the request will be rejected with authentication failed error (401). Leave the list empty if origin authentication is not required.
---@field peers? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.PeerAuthenticationMethodList List of authentication methods that can be used for peer authentication. They will be evaluated in order the first valid one will be used to set peer identity. If none of these methods pass, the request will be rejected with authentication failed error (401). Leave the list empty if peer authentication is not required.
---@field principalBinding? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuthenticationPolicyPrincipalBindingEnum|string Define whether peer or origin identity should be used for principal. Default value is USE_PEER. If peer (or origin) identity is not available, either because peer/origin authentication is not defined, or failed, principal will be left unset. In other words, binding rule does not affect the decision to accept or reject request. This field can be set to one of the following: USE_PEER: Principal will be set to the identity from peer authentication. USE_ORIGIN: Principal will be set to the identity from origin authentication.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuthenticationPolicyPrincipalBindingEnum "INVALID"|"USE_ORIGIN"|"USE_PEER"

