---Groups information about a shard of capacity.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CapacityAdviceResponseRecommendationScores
---@field obtainability? number The obtainability score indicates the likelihood of successfully obtaining (provisioning) the requested number of VMs. The score range is 0.0 through 1.0. Higher is better.
---@field estimatedWaitDuration? string Output only. The likely maximum time that you will have to wait until Compute Engine provisions your instances.
---@field uptimeScore? number The uptime score indicates the likelihood that your Spot VMs will continue to run without preemption within the next few hours. For more information about the preemption process, see Preemption of Spot VMs. The score range is 0.0 through 1.0. Higher is better.
---@field estimatedUptime? string The estimated run time of the majority of Spot VMs in the request before preemption. The estimate is best-effort only. It is based on historical data and current conditions.

---Shards represent blocks of uniform capacity in recommendations.
---Each shard is for a single zone and a single machine shape. Each shard
---defines a size expressed as the number of VMs.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CapacityAdviceResponseRecommendationShard
---@field instanceCount? number The number of instances.
---@field zone? string Output only. The zone name for this shard.
---@field provisioningModel? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CapacityAdviceResponseRecommendationShardProvisioningModelEnum The provisioning model that you want to view recommendations for.
---@field machineType? string The machine type corresponds to the instance selection in the request.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CapacityAdviceResponseRecommendationShardList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CapacityAdviceResponseRecommendationShard[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CapacityAdviceResponseRecommendationShardProvisioningModelEnum "FLEX_START"|"RESERVATION_BOUND"|"SPOT"|"STANDARD"

