---HaController handles failover for a VM Instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HaController
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HaControllerStateEnum Output only. The current state of the HA Controller.
---@field zoneConfigurations? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HaControllerZoneConfigurationMap Map of zone configurations Key: name of the zone Value: ZoneConfiguration
---@field backendServices? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Advanced configuration option. If specified, these Backend Services need to be pre-created. Currently, only one backend service can be specified, and it must be L4 Internal Load Balancer (ILB).
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HaControllerStatus Output only. [Output Only] Status information for the HaController resource.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field instanceName? string Name of the instance that HaController is in charge of. If not specified the HaController's resource name will be used instead. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field networkingAutoConfiguration? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HaControllerNetworkingAutoConfiguration Basic networking configuration. Required backend services and forwarding rules will be automatically created with default parameters.
