---Represents a health check resource.
---
---Google Compute Engine has two health check resources:
---
---* [Regional](/compute/docs/reference/rest/alpha/regionHealthChecks)
---* [Global](/compute/docs/reference/rest/alpha/healthChecks)
---
---These health check resources can be used for load balancing and for
---autohealing VMs in a managed instance group (MIG).
---
---**Load balancing**
---
---Health check requirements vary depending on the type of load balancer. For
---details about the type of health check supported for
---each load balancer and corresponding backend type,
---see Health
---checks overview: Load balancer guide.
---
---**Autohealing in MIGs**
---
---The health checks that you use for autohealing VMs in a MIG can be either
---regional or global. For more information, see  Set up an
---application health check and autohealing.
---
---For more information, seeHealth checks
---overview.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HealthCheck
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HealthCheckTypeEnum Specifies the type of the healthCheck, either TCP,SSL, HTTP, HTTPS,HTTP2, GRPC or GRPC_WITH_TLS. Exactly one of the protocol-specific health check fields must be specified, which must match type field.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp in3339 text format.
---@field udpHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UDPHealthCheck
---@field grpcTlsHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.GRPCTLSHealthCheck
---@field checkIntervalSec? number How often (in seconds) to send a health check. The default value is 5 seconds.
---@field httpsHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HTTPSHealthCheck
---@field grpcHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.GRPCHealthCheck
---@field id? string [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field timeoutSec? number How long (in seconds) to wait before claiming failure. The default value is 5 seconds. It is invalid for timeoutSec to have greater value than checkIntervalSec.
---@field kind? string Output only. Type of the resource.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field logConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HealthCheckLogConfig Configure logging on this health check.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. For example, a name that is 1-63 characters long, matches the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?`, and otherwise complies with RFC1035. This regular expression describes a name where the first character is a lowercase letter, and all following characters are a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which isn't a dash.
---@field httpHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HTTPHealthCheck
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field unhealthyThreshold? number A so-far healthy instance will be marked unhealthy after this many consecutive failures. The default value is 2.
---@field selfLink? string [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field sourceRegions? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList The list of cloud regions from which health checks are performed. If any regions are specified, then exactly 3 regions should be specified. The region names must be valid names of Google Cloud regions. This can only be set for global health check. If this list is non-empty, then there are restrictions on what other health check fields are supported and what other resources can use this health check: - SSL, HTTP2, GRPC, and GRPC_WITH_TLS protocols are not supported. - The TCP request field is not supported. - The proxyHeader field for HTTP, HTTPS, and TCP is not supported. - The checkIntervalSec field must be at least 30. - The health check cannot be used with BackendService nor with managed instance group auto-healing.
---@field sslHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SSLHealthCheck
---@field region? string Output only. [Output Only] Region where the health check resides. Not applicable to global health checks.
---@field http2HealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.HTTP2HealthCheck
---@field healthyThreshold? number A so-far unhealthy instance will be marked healthy after this many consecutive successes. The default value is 2.
---@field tcpHealthCheck? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.TCPHealthCheck

