---Represents an Instance resource.
---
---An instance is a virtual machine that is hosted on Google Cloud Platform.
---For more information, readVirtual Machine Instances.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Instance
---@field upcomingMaintenance? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpcomingMaintenance Output only. [Output Only] DEPRECATED: Please useresource_status.upcoming_maintenance instead. Specifies upcoming maintenance for the instance.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource.
---@field minCpuPlatform? string Specifies aminimum CPU platform for the VM instance. Applicable values are the friendly names of CPU platforms, such as minCpuPlatform: "Intel Haswell" or minCpuPlatform: "Intel Sandy Bridge".
---@field instanceEncryptionKey? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CustomerEncryptionKey Encrypts suspended data for an instance with acustomer-managed encryption key. If you are creating a new instance, this field will encrypt the local SSD and in-memory contents of the instance during the suspend operation. If you do not provide an encryption key when creating the instance, then the local SSD and in-memory contents will be encrypted using an automatically generated key during the suspend operation.
---@field keyRevocationActionType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum KeyRevocationActionType of the instance. Supported options are "STOP" and "NONE". The default value is "NONE" if it is not specified.
---@field networkInterfaces? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkInterfaceList An array of network configurations for this instance. These specify how interfaces are configured to interact with other network services, such as connecting to the internet. Multiple interfaces are supported per instance.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field fingerprint? string Specifies a fingerprint for this resource, which is essentially a hash of the instance's contents and used for optimistic locking. The fingerprint is initially generated by Compute Engine and changes after every request to modify or update the instance. You must always provide an up-to-date fingerprint hash in order to update the instance. To see the latest fingerprint, make get() request to the instance.
---@field shieldedVmIntegrityPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShieldedVmIntegrityPolicy Output only. Deprecating, please use shielded_instance_integrity_policy.
---@field zone? string Output only. [Output Only] URL of the zone where the instance resides. You must specify this field as part of the HTTP request URL. It is not settable as a field in the request body.
---@field lastStartTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Last start timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field guestAccelerators? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AcceleratorConfigList A list of the type and count of accelerator cards attached to the instance.
---@field shieldedVmConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShieldedVmConfig Output only. Deprecating, please use shielded_instance_config.
---@field scheduling? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Scheduling Sets the scheduling options for this instance.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap Labels to apply to this instance. These can be later modified by the setLabels method.
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Reserved for future use.
---@field deletionProtection? boolean Whether the resource should be protected against deletion.
---@field postKeyRevocationActionType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePostKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum PostKeyRevocationActionType of the instance.
---@field serviceIntegrationSpecs? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ServiceIntegrationSpecMap Mapping of user-defined keys to specifications for service integrations. Currently only a single key-value pair is supported.
---@field startRestricted? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Whether a VM has been restricted for start because Compute Engine has detected suspicious activity.
---@field shieldedInstanceIntegrityPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShieldedInstanceIntegrityPolicy
---@field displayDevice? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.DisplayDevice Enables display device for the instance.
---@field serviceAccounts? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ServiceAccountList A list of service accounts, with their specified scopes, authorized for this instance. Only one service account per VM instance is supported. Service accounts generate access tokens that can be accessed through the metadata server and used to authenticate applications on the instance. SeeService Accounts for more information.
---@field name? string The name of the resource, provided by the client when initially creating the resource. The resource name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceParams Input only. [Input Only] Additional params passed with the request, but not persisted as part of resource payload.
---@field statusMessage? string Output only. [Output Only] An optional, human-readable explanation of the status.
---@field identityCertificate? boolean
---@field canIpForward? boolean Allows this instance to send and receive packets with non-matching destination or source IPs. This is required if you plan to use this instance to forward routes. For more information, seeEnabling IP Forwarding.
---@field reservationAffinity? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAffinity Specifies the reservations that this instance can consume from.
---@field disks? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AttachedDiskList Array of disks associated with this instance. Persistent disks must be created before you can assign them.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Always compute#instance for instances.
---@field sourceMachineImageEncryptionKey? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CustomerEncryptionKey Source machine image encryption key when creating an instance from a machine image.
---@field workloadIdentityConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.WorkloadIdentityConfig
---@field sourceMachineImage? string Source machine image
---@field preservedStateSizeGb? string Output only. Total amount of preserved state for SUSPENDED instances. Read-only in the api.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field resourceStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ResourceStatus Output only. [Output Only] Specifies values set for instance attributes as compared to the values requested by user in the corresponding input only field.
---@field localSsdEncryptionMode? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceLocalSsdEncryptionModeEnum Specifies which method should be used for encrypting the Local SSDs attached to the VM.
---@field resourcePolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Resource policies applied to this instance.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field secureTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList [Input Only] Secure tags to apply to this instance. These can be later modified by the update method. Maximum number of secure tags allowed is 50.
---@field networkPerformanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPerformanceConfig
---@field machineType? string Full or partial URL of the machine type resource to use for this instance, in the format:zones/zone/machineTypes/machine-type. This is provided by the client when the instance is created. For example, the following is a valid partial url to a predefined machine type: zones/us-central1-f/machineTypes/n1-standard-1 To create acustom machine type, provide a URL to a machine type in the following format, where CPUS is 1 or an even number up to 32 (2, 4, 6, ... 24, etc), and MEMORY is the total memory for this instance. Memory must be a multiple of 256 MB and must be supplied in MB (e.g. 5 GB of memory is 5120 MB): zones/zone/machineTypes/custom-CPUS-MEMORY For example: zones/us-central1-f/machineTypes/custom-4-5120 For a full list of restrictions, read theSpecifications for custom machine types.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Metadata The metadata key/value pairs assigned to this instance. This includes metadata keys that were explicitly defined for the instance.
---@field managementInterfaces? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceMap Map of management interfaces. Keys must be valid RFC1035 names and at most 63 characters long.
---@field confidentialInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ConfidentialInstanceConfig
---@field eraseWindowsVssSignature? boolean Specifies whether the disks restored from source snapshots or source machine image should erase Windows specific VSS signature.
