---Represents Out-of-Band (OOB) Host Management Interface configuration
---details for direct host control.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterface
---@field ipv4Address? string The IPv4 internal IP address assigned to this management interface endpoint. This address will be used by the customer to route traffic to the management interface.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceTypeEnum|string Required. The type of management service this interface provides. Supported types include HOST_MANAGEMENT for direct host control.
---@field subnetwork? string The URL of the subnetwork from which to assign the IP address for the endpoint. The subnetwork must belong to the specified network and have available IP addresses.
---@field network? string The URL of the VPC network to which the management interface endpoint is attached. The customer must ensure that this network is correctly configured for routing to the instance.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceStateEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] The current state of the management interface endpoint.
---@field ipv6Address? string The IPv6 internal IP address assigned to this management interface endpoint. This address will be used by the customer to route traffic to the management interface if IPv6 is supported and configured.
---@field authenticationConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceAuthenticationConfig The authentication configuration for secure connection.

---Authentication configuration for the management interface, typically
---using mTLS.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceAuthenticationConfig
---@field trustConfig? string Required. Resource name of the Cloud Certificate Manager TrustConfig used to validate client certificates for mTLS. Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/trustConfigs/{trust_config}

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterface }

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceStateEnum "ACTIVE"|"INACTIVE"|"PENDING"|"STATE_UNSPECIFIED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceManagementInterfaceTypeEnum "HOST_MANAGEMENT"|"TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"

---Additional instance params.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceParams
---@field resourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap Input only. Resource manager tags to be bound to the instance. Tag keys and values have the same definition as resource manager tags. Keys and values can be either in numeric format, such as `tagKeys/{tag_key_id}` and `tagValues/{tag_value_id}` or in namespaced format such as `{org_id|project_id}/{tag_key_short_name}` and `{tag_value_short_name}`. The field is ignored (both PUT & PATCH) when empty.
---@field requestValidForDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Duration Relative deadline for waiting for capacity. Relevant only for Instances.Insert API.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePostKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum "NOOP"|"POST_KEY_REVOCATION_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SHUTDOWN"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum "ENABLE_BIDIRECTIONAL_ACCESS_TO_GOOGLE"|"ENABLE_OUTBOUND_VM_ACCESS_TO_GOOGLE"|"INHERIT_FROM_SUBNETWORK"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceProperties
---@field guestAccelerators? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AcceleratorConfigList A list of guest accelerator cards' type and count to use for instances created from these properties.
---@field keyRevocationActionType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum|string KeyRevocationActionType of the instance. Supported options are "STOP" and "NONE". The default value is "NONE" if it is not specified.
---@field serviceAccounts? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ServiceAccountList A list of service accounts with specified scopes. Access tokens for these service accounts are available to the instances that are created from these properties. Use metadata queries to obtain the access tokens for these instances.
---@field shieldedVmConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShieldedVmConfig Specifies the Shielded VM options for the instances that are created from these properties.
---@field shieldedInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShieldedInstanceConfig Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field networkPerformanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPerformanceConfig Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field reservationAffinity? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAffinity Specifies the reservations that instances can consume from. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field tags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Tags A list of tags to apply to the instances that are created from these properties. The tags identify valid sources or targets for network firewalls. The setTags method can modify this list of tags. Each tag within the list must comply with RFC1035.
---@field privateIpv6GoogleAccess? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesPrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum|string The private IPv6 google access type for VMs. If not specified, use INHERIT_FROM_SUBNETWORK as default. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field identityCertificate? boolean
---@field workloadIdentityConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.WorkloadIdentityConfig
---@field resourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap Input only. Resource manager tags to be bound to the instance. Tag keys and values have the same definition as resource manager tags. Keys and values can be either in numeric format, such as `tagKeys/{tag_key_id}` and `tagValues/{tag_value_id}` or in namespaced format such as `{org_id|project_id}/{tag_key_short_name}` and `{tag_value_short_name}`. The field is ignored (both PUT & PATCH) when empty.
---@field networkInterfaces? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkInterfaceList An array of network access configurations for this interface.
---@field serviceIntegrationSpecs? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ServiceIntegrationSpecMap Mapping of user defined keys to ServiceIntegrationSpec.
---@field resourcePolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Resource policies (names, not URLs) applied to instances created from these properties. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field minCpuPlatform? string Minimum cpu/platform to be used by instances. The instance may be scheduled on the specified or newer cpu/platform. Applicable values are the friendly names of CPU platforms, such asminCpuPlatform: "Intel Haswell" orminCpuPlatform: "Intel Sandy Bridge". For more information, read Specifying a Minimum CPU Platform.
---@field advancedMachineFeatures? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AdvancedMachineFeatures Controls for advanced machine-related behavior features. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field localSsdEncryptionMode? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesLocalSsdEncryptionModeEnum|string Specifies which method should be used for encrypting the Local SSDs attached to the VM.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Metadata The metadata key/value pairs to assign to instances that are created from these properties. These pairs can consist of custom metadata or predefined keys. SeeProject and instance metadata for more information.
---@field displayDevice? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.DisplayDevice Display Device properties to enable support for remote display products like: Teradici, VNC and TeamViewer Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field scheduling? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Scheduling Specifies the scheduling options for the instances that are created from these properties.
---@field canIpForward? boolean Enables instances created based on these properties to send packets with source IP addresses other than their own and receive packets with destination IP addresses other than their own. If these instances will be used as an IP gateway or it will be set as the next-hop in a Route resource, specify true. If unsure, leave this set tofalse. See theEnable IP forwarding documentation for more information.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap Labels to apply to instances that are created from these properties.
---@field confidentialInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ConfidentialInstanceConfig Specifies the Confidential Instance options. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field machineType? string The machine type to use for instances that are created from these properties. This field only accepts a machine type name, for example `n2-standard-4`. If you use the machine type full or partial URL, for example `projects/my-l7ilb-project/zones/us-central1-a/machineTypes/n2-standard-4`, the request will result in an `INTERNAL_ERROR`.
---@field postKeyRevocationActionType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesPostKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum|string PostKeyRevocationActionType of the instance.
---@field secureTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList [Input Only] Secure tags to apply to this instance. Maximum number of secure tags allowed is 50. Note that for MachineImage, this is not supported yet.
---@field partnerMetadata? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StructuredEntriesMap Partner Metadata assigned to the instance properties. A map from a subdomain (namespace) to entries map.
---@field description? string An optional text description for the instances that are created from these properties.
---@field identity? string
---@field disks? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AttachedDiskList An array of disks that are associated with the instances that are created from these properties.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum "KEY_REVOCATION_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"STOP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesLocalSsdEncryptionModeEnum "CMEK_ENCRYPTION"|"EPHEMERAL_KEY_ENCRYPTION"|"LOCAL_SSD_ENCRYPTION_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STANDARD_ENCRYPTION"

---Represents the change that you want to make to the instance properties.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesPatch
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap The metadata key-value pairs that you want to patch onto the instance. For more information, see Project and instance metadata.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap The label key-value pairs that you want to patch onto the instance.
---@field exposeHostTopology? boolean This optional flag exposes the hashed physical host ID.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesPostKeyRevocationActionTypeEnum "NOOP"|"POST_KEY_REVOCATION_ACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SHUTDOWN"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePropertiesPrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum "ENABLE_BIDIRECTIONAL_ACCESS_TO_GOOGLE"|"ENABLE_OUTBOUND_VM_ACCESS_TO_GOOGLE"|"INHERIT_FROM_SUBNETWORK"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceReference
---@field instance? string The URL for a specific instance. @required compute.instancegroups.addInstances/removeInstances

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceReferenceList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceReference[]

---Represents a Instance Settings resource. You can use instance settings to
