---L2 Interconnect Attachment related configuration.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2Forwarding
---@field tunnelEndpointIpAddress? string Required. A single IPv4 or IPv6 address. This address will be used as the source IP address for packets sent to the appliances, and must be used as the destination IP address for packets that should be sent out through this attachment.
---@field geneveHeader? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingGeneveHeader Optional. It represents the structure of a Geneve (Generic Network Virtualization Encapsulation) header, as defined in RFC8926. It encapsulates packets from various protocols (e.g., Ethernet, IPv4, IPv6) for use in network virtualization environments.
---@field applianceMappings? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMappingMap Optional. A map of VLAN tags to appliances and optional inner mapping rules. If VLANs are not explicitly mapped to any appliance, the defaultApplianceIpAddress is used. Each VLAN tag can be a single number or a range of numbers in the range of 1 to 4094, e.g., "1" or "4001-4094". Non-empty and non-overlapping VLAN tag ranges are enforced, and violating operations will be rejected. The VLAN tags in the Ethernet header must use an ethertype value of 0x88A8 or 0x8100.
---@field defaultApplianceIpAddress? string Optional. A single IPv4 or IPv6 address used as the default destination IP when there is no VLAN mapping result found. Unset field (null-value) indicates the unmatched packet should be dropped.
---@field network? string Required. Resource URL of the network to which this attachment belongs.

---Two-level VLAN-to-Appliance mapping rule.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMapping
---@field name? string Optional. The name of this appliance mapping rule.
---@field innerVlanToApplianceMappings? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMappingInnerVlanToApplianceMappingList Optional. Used to match against the inner VLAN when the packet contains two VLAN tags. A list of mapping rules from inner VLAN tags to IP addresses. If the inner VLAN is not explicitly mapped to an IP address range, the applianceIpAddress is used.
---@field applianceIpAddress? string Optional. A single IPv4 or IPv6 address used as the destination IP address for ingress packets that match on a VLAN tag, but do not match a more specific inner VLAN tag. Unset field (null-value) indicates both VLAN tags are required to be mapped. Otherwise, defaultApplianceIpAddress is used.

---The inner VLAN-to-Appliance mapping.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMappingInnerVlanToApplianceMapping
---@field innerVlanTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Required in this object. Used to match the inner VLAN tag on the packet. Each entry can be a single number or a range of numbers in the range of 1 to 4094, e.g., ["1", "4001-4094"] is valid. Non-empty and Non-overlapping VLAN tag ranges are enforced, and violating operations will be rejected. The inner VLAN tags must have an ethertype value of 0x8100.
---@field innerApplianceIpAddress? string Required in this object. A single IPv4 or IPv6 address used as the destination IP address for ingress packets that match on both VLAN tags.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMappingInnerVlanToApplianceMappingList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMappingInnerVlanToApplianceMapping[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMappingMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingApplianceMapping }

---GeneveHeader related configurations.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentL2ForwardingGeneveHeader
---@field vni? number Optional. VNI is a 24-bit unique virtual network identifier, from 0 to 16,777,215.

