---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPower
---@field value? number Value of the current receiving or transmitting optical power, read in dBm. Take a known good optical value, give it a 10% margin and trigger warnings relative to that value. In general, a -7dBm warning and a -11dBm alarm are good optical value estimates for most links.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPowerStateEnum The status of the current value when compared to the warning and alarm levels for the receiving or transmitting transceiver. Possible states include: - OK: The value has not crossed a warning threshold. - LOW_WARNING: The value has crossed below the low warning threshold. - HIGH_WARNING: The value has crossed above the high warning threshold. - LOW_ALARM: The value has crossed below the low alarm threshold. - HIGH_ALARM: The value has crossed above the high alarm threshold.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPowerStateEnum "HIGH_ALARM"|"HIGH_WARNING"|"LOW_ALARM"|"LOW_WARNING"|"OK"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatus
---@field arpCaches? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsARPEntryList A list of InterconnectDiagnostics.ARPEntry objects, describing the ARP neighbor entries seen on this link. This will be empty if the link is bundled
---@field operationalStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatusOperationalStatusEnum The operational status of the link.
---@field transmittingOpticalPower? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPower An InterconnectDiagnostics.LinkOpticalPower object, describing the current value and status of the transmitted light level.
---@field googleDemarc? string The Demarc address assigned by Google and provided in the LoA.
---@field macsec? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsMacsecStatus Describes the status of MACsec encryption on this link.
---@field receivingOpticalPower? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkOpticalPower An InterconnectDiagnostics.LinkOpticalPower object, describing the current value and status of the received light level.
---@field lacpStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkLACPStatus
---@field circuitId? string The unique ID for this link assigned during turn up by Google.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatusList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatus[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsLinkStatusOperationalStatusEnum "LINK_OPERATIONAL_STATUS_DOWN"|"LINK_OPERATIONAL_STATUS_UP"

---Describes the status of MACsec encryption on the link.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectDiagnosticsMacsecStatus
---@field ckn? string Indicates the Connectivity Association Key Name (CKN) currently being used if MACsec is operational.
---@field operational? boolean Indicates whether or not MACsec is operational on this link.

---An interconnect group resource allows customers to create, analyze, and
---expand their redundant connections.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroup
---@field configured? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupConfigured
---@field intent? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupIntent
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource type. The server generates this identifier.
---@field physicalStructure? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupPhysicalStructure
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Always compute#InterconnectGroup
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field etag? string Opaque system-generated token that uniquely identifies the configuration. If provided when patching a configuration in update mode, the provided token must match the current token or the update is rejected. This provides a reliable means of doing read-modify-write (optimistic locking) as described by AIP 154.
---@field interconnects? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupInterconnectMap Interconnects in the InterconnectGroup. Keys are arbitrary user-specified strings. Users are encouraged, but not required, to use their preferred format for resource links as keys. Note that there are add-members and remove-members methods in gcloud. The size of this map is limited by an "Interconnects per group" quota.

---[Output Only] The status of the group as configured. This has the same
---structure as the operational field reported by the OperationalStatus
---method, but does not take into account the operational status of each
---resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupConfigured
---@field topologyCapability? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupConfiguredTopologyCapability

---[Output Only] How reliable this topology is configured to be, and why
---this group does or does not meet the requirements for the intended
---capability.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupConfiguredTopologyCapability
---@field supportedSla? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupConfiguredTopologyCapabilitySupportedSlaEnum|string
---@field intendedCapabilityBlockers? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupConfiguredTopologyCapabilityIntendedCapabilityBlockersList

---[Output Only] Reasons why configuration.topologyCapability.sla differs
---from intent.topologyCapability. This list is empty if and only if those
---are the same.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectGroupConfiguredTopologyCapabilityIntendedCapabilityBlockers
