---Creating VLAN Attachments.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectLocation
---@field availableFeatures? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectLocationAvailableFeaturesItemEnumList [Output only] List of features available at this InterconnectLocation, which can take one of the following values: - IF_MACSEC - IF_CROSS_SITE_NETWORK
---@field name? string Output only. [Output Only] Name of the resource.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field singleRegionProductionCriticalPeerLocations? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. [Output Only] URLs of the other locations that can pair up with this location to support Single-Region 99.99% SLA. E.g. iad-zone1-1 and iad-zone2-5467 are Single-Region 99.99% peer locations of each other.
---@field description? string Output only. [Output Only] An optional description of the resource.
---@field facilityProvider? string Output only. [Output Only] The name of the provider for this facility (e.g., EQUINIX).
---@field availabilityZone? string [Output Only] Availability zone for this InterconnectLocation. Within a metropolitan area (metro), maintenance will not be simultaneously scheduled in more than one availability zone. Example: "zone1" or "zone2".
---@field address? string Output only. [Output Only] The postal address of the Point of Presence, each line in the address is separated by a newline character.
---@field supportsPzs? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Reserved for future use.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectLocationStatusEnum [Output Only] The status of this InterconnectLocation, which can take one of the following values: - CLOSED: The InterconnectLocation is closed and is unavailable for provisioning new Interconnects. - AVAILABLE: The InterconnectLocation is available for provisioning new Interconnects.
---@field availableLinkTypes? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectLocationAvailableLinkTypesItemEnumList [Output only] List of link types available at this InterconnectLocation, which can take one of the following values: - LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_10G_LR - LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_100G_LR - LINK_TYPE_ETHERNET_400G_LR4
---@field regionInfos? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectLocationRegionInfoList Output only. [Output Only] A list of InterconnectLocation.RegionInfo objects, that describe parameters pertaining to the relation between this InterconnectLocation and various Google Cloud regions.
---@field peeringdbFacilityId? string Output only. [Output Only] The peeringdb identifier for this facility (corresponding with a netfac type in peeringdb).
---@field facilityProviderFacilityId? string Output only. [Output Only] A provider-assigned Identifier for this facility (e.g., Ashburn-DC1).
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#interconnectLocation for interconnect locations.
---@field continent? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectLocationContinentEnum [Output Only] Continent for this location, which can take one of the following values: - AFRICA - ASIA_PAC - EUROPE - NORTH_AMERICA - SOUTH_AMERICA
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field crossSiteInterconnectInfos? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectLocationCrossSiteInterconnectInfoList [Output Only] A list of InterconnectLocation.CrossSiteInterconnectInfo objects, that describe where Cross-Site Interconnect wires may connect to from this location and associated connection parameters. Cross-Site Interconnect isn't allowed to locations which are not listed.
---@field city? string [Output Only] Metropolitan area designator that indicates which city an interconnect is located. For example: "Chicago, IL", "Amsterdam, Netherlands".
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.

