---Configuration information for enabling Media Access Control security
---(MACsec) on this Cloud Interconnect connection between Google and your
---on-premises router.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsec
---@field failOpen? boolean If set to true, the Interconnect connection is configured with ashould-secure MACsec security policy, that allows the Google router to fallback to cleartext traffic if the MKA session cannot be established. By default, the Interconnect connection is configured with amust-secure security policy that drops all traffic if the MKA session cannot be established with your router.
---@field interconnectKeyGroup? string Optional. URL of the InterconnectKeyGroup resource to use for MACsec, in the format: projects/{project}/locations/{region}/interconnectKeyGroups/{interconnectKeyGroup}.
---@field preSharedKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKeyList Required. A keychain placeholder describing a set of named key objects along with their start times. A MACsec CKN/CAK is generated for each key in the key chain. Google router automatically picks the key with the most recent startTime when establishing or re-establishing a MACsec secure link.

---MACsec configuration information for the Interconnect connection. Contains
---the generated Connectivity Association Key Name (CKN) and the key (CAK) for
---this Interconnect connection.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecConfig
---@field preSharedKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKeyList A keychain placeholder describing a set of named key objects along with their start times. A MACsec CKN/CAK is generated for each key in the key chain. Google router automatically picks the key with the most recent startTime when establishing or re-establishing a MACsec secure link.

---Describes a pre-shared key used to setup MACsec in static connectivity
---association key (CAK) mode.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKey
---@field startTime? string User provided timestamp on or after which this key is valid.
---@field cak? string An auto-generated Connectivity Association Key (CAK) for this key.
---@field name? string User provided name for this pre-shared key.
---@field ckn? string An auto-generated Connectivity Association Key Name (CKN) for this key.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKeyList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecConfigPreSharedKey[]

---Describes a pre-shared key used to setup MACsec in static connectivity
---association key (CAK) mode.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKey
---@field name? string Required. A name for this pre-shared key. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field startTime? string A RFC3339 timestamp on or after which the key is valid. startTime can be in the future. If the keychain has a single key, startTime can be omitted. If the keychain has multiple keys, startTime is mandatory for each key. The start times of keys must be in increasing order. The start times of two consecutive keys must be at least 6 hours apart.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKeyList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectMacsecPreSharedKey[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOperationalStatusEnum "OS_ACTIVE"|"OS_UNPROVISIONED"

---Description of a planned outage on this Interconnect.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotification
---@field startTime? string Scheduled start time for the outage (milliseconds since Unix epoch).
---@field endTime? string Scheduled end time for the outage (milliseconds since Unix epoch).
---@field affectedCircuits? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList If issue_type is IT_PARTIAL_OUTAGE, a list of the Google-side circuit IDs that will be affected.
---@field description? string A description about the purpose of the outage.
---@field name? string Unique identifier for this outage notification.
---@field issueType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotificationIssueTypeEnum|string Form this outage is expected to take, which can take one of the following values: - OUTAGE: The Interconnect may be completely out of service for some or all of the specified window. - PARTIAL_OUTAGE: Some circuits comprising the Interconnect as a whole should remain up, but with reduced bandwidth. Note that the versions of this enum prefixed with "IT_" have been deprecated in favor of the unprefixed values.
---@field source? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotificationSourceEnum|string The party that generated this notification, which can take the following value: - GOOGLE: this notification as generated by Google. Note that the value of NSRC_GOOGLE has been deprecated in favor of GOOGLE.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotificationStateEnum|string State of this notification, which can take one of the following values: - ACTIVE: This outage notification is active. The event could be in the past, present, or future. See start_time and end_time for scheduling. - CANCELLED: The outage associated with this notification was cancelled before the outage was due to start. - COMPLETED: The outage associated with this notification is complete. Note that the versions of this enum prefixed with "NS_" have been deprecated in favor of the unprefixed values.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotificationIssueTypeEnum "IT_OUTAGE"|"IT_PARTIAL_OUTAGE"|"OUTAGE"|"PARTIAL_OUTAGE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotificationList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotification[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotificationSourceEnum "GOOGLE"|"NSRC_GOOGLE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectOutageNotificationStateEnum "ACTIVE"|"CANCELLED"|"COMPLETED"|"NS_ACTIVE"|"NS_CANCELED"

---Additional interconnect parameters.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectParams
---@field resourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap Tag keys/values directly bound to this resource. Tag keys and values have the same definition as resource manager tags. The field is allowed for INSERT only. The keys/values to set on the resource should be specified in either ID { : } or Namespaced format { : }. For example the following are valid inputs: * {"tagKeys/333" : "tagValues/444", "tagKeys/123" : "tagValues/456"} * {"123/environment" : "production", "345/abc" : "xyz"} Note: * Invalid combinations of ID & namespaced format is not supported. For instance: {"123/environment" : "tagValues/444"} is invalid. * Inconsistent format is not supported. For instance: {"tagKeys/333" : "tagValues/444", "123/env" : "prod"} is invalid.

---Represents a Cross-Cloud Interconnect Remote Location resource.
---
---You can use this resource to find remote location details about an
---Interconnect attachment (VLAN).
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocation
---@field address? string Output only. [Output Only] The postal address of the Point of Presence, each line in the address is separated by a newline character.
---@field facilityProviderFacilityId? string Output only. [Output Only] A provider-assigned Identifier for this facility (e.g., Ashburn-DC1).
---@field maxLagSize400Gbps? number Output only. [Output Only] The maximum number of 400 Gbps ports supported in a link aggregation group (LAG). When linkType is 400 Gbps, requestedLinkCount cannot exceed max_lag_size_400_gbps.
---@field constraints? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraints Output only. [Output Only] Constraints on the parameters for creating Cross-Cloud Interconnect and associated InterconnectAttachments.
---@field peeringdbFacilityId? string Output only. [Output Only] The peeringdb identifier for this facility (corresponding with a netfac type in peeringdb).
---@field remoteService? string Output only. [Output Only] Indicates the service provider present at the remote location. Example values: "Amazon Web Services", "Microsoft Azure".
---@field name? string Output only. [Output Only] Name of the resource.
---@field facilityProvider? string Output only. [Output Only] The name of the provider for this facility (e.g., EQUINIX).
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#interconnectRemoteLocation for interconnect remote locations.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field lacp? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationLacpEnum Output only. [Output Only] Link Aggregation Control Protocol (LACP) constraints, which can take one of the following values: LACP_SUPPORTED, LACP_UNSUPPORTED
---@field permittedConnections? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationPermittedConnectionsList Output only. [Output Only] Permitted connections.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field description? string Output only. [Output Only] An optional description of the resource.
---@field continent? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationContinentEnum Output only. [Output Only] Continent for this location, which can take one of the following values: - AFRICA - ASIA_PAC - EUROPE - NORTH_AMERICA - SOUTH_AMERICA
---@field city? string Output only. [Output Only] Metropolitan area designator that indicates which city an interconnect is located. For example: "Chicago, IL", "Amsterdam, Netherlands".
---@field maxLagSize10Gbps? number Output only. [Output Only] The maximum number of 10 Gbps ports supported in a link aggregation group (LAG). When linkType is 10 Gbps, requestedLinkCount cannot exceed max_lag_size_10_gbps.
---@field maxLagSize100Gbps? number Output only. [Output Only] The maximum number of 100 Gbps ports supported in a link aggregation group (LAG). When linkType is 100 Gbps, requestedLinkCount cannot exceed max_lag_size_100_gbps.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationStatusEnum Output only. [Output Only] The status of this InterconnectRemoteLocation, which can take one of the following values: - CLOSED: The InterconnectRemoteLocation is closed and is unavailable for provisioning new Cross-Cloud Interconnects. - AVAILABLE: The InterconnectRemoteLocation is available for provisioning new Cross-Cloud Interconnects.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field attachmentConfigurationConstraints? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectAttachmentConfigurationConstraints Output only. [Output Only] Subset of fields from InterconnectAttachment's |configurationConstraints| field that apply to all attachments for this remote location.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraints
---@field subnetLengthRange? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraintsSubnetLengthRange Output only. [Output Only] [min-length, max-length] The minimum and maximum value (inclusive) for the IPv4 subnet length. For example, an interconnectRemoteLocation for Azure has {min: 30, max: 30} because Azure requires /30 subnets. This range specifies the values supported by both cloud providers. Interconnect currently supports /29 and /30 IPv4 subnet lengths. If a remote cloud has no constraint on IPv4 subnet length, the range would thus be {min: 29, max: 30}.
---@field portPairRemoteLocation? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraintsPortPairRemoteLocationEnum Output only. [Output Only] Port pair remote location constraints, which can take one of the following values: PORT_PAIR_UNCONSTRAINED_REMOTE_LOCATION, PORT_PAIR_MATCHING_REMOTE_LOCATION. Google Cloud API refers only to individual ports, but the UI uses this field when ordering a pair of ports, to prevent users from accidentally ordering something that is incompatible with their cloud provider. Specifically, when ordering a redundant pair of Cross-Cloud Interconnect ports, and one of them uses a remote location with portPairMatchingRemoteLocation set to matching, the UI requires that both ports use the same remote location.
---@field portPairVlan? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraintsPortPairVlanEnum Output only. [Output Only] Port pair VLAN constraints, which can take one of the following values: PORT_PAIR_UNCONSTRAINED_VLAN, PORT_PAIR_MATCHING_VLAN

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraintsPortPairRemoteLocationEnum "PORT_PAIR_MATCHING_REMOTE_LOCATION"|"PORT_PAIR_UNCONSTRAINED_REMOTE_LOCATION"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraintsPortPairVlanEnum "PORT_PAIR_MATCHING_VLAN"|"PORT_PAIR_UNCONSTRAINED_VLAN"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InterconnectRemoteLocationConstraintsSubnetLengthRange
---@field max? number
---@field min? number

