---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocalDisk
---@field diskCount? number Specifies the number of such disks.
---@field diskType? string Specifies the desired disk type on the node. This disk type must be a local storage type (e.g.: local-ssd). Note that for nodeTemplates, this should be the name of the disk type and not its URL.
---@field diskSizeGb? number Specifies the size of the disk in base-2 GB.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocalDiskList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocalDisk[]

---Provides a localized error message that is safe to return to the user
---which can be attached to an RPC error.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocalizedMessage
---@field locale? string The locale used following the specification defined at https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/bcp/bcp47.txt. Examples are: "en-US", "fr-CH", "es-MX"
---@field message? string The localized error message in the above locale.

---Configuration for location policy among multiple possible locations
---(e.g. preferences for zone selection among zones in a single region).
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicy
---@field zones? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyZoneConfigurationList The bulkInsert operation applies any preferences set in the locations field to the specific zones listed in the zones field if the same zones are specified in both fields.
---@field targetShape? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyTargetShapeEnum|string Strategy for distributing VMs across zones in a region.
---@field locations? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocationMap Location configurations mapped by location name. Currently only zone names are supported and must be represented as valid internal URLs, such as zones/us-central1-a. The bulkInsert operation doesn't create instances in an AI zone, even if an AI zone is available in the specified region. For example, if you set a DENY preference for us-central1-a, Compute Engine will consider us-central1-b and us-central1-c for instance creation, but not us-central1-ai1a. Also, you can't use the locations[] configuration to allow instance creation in an AI zone. To include an AI zone in bulkInsert operations, use the locationPolicy.zones[] field.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocation
---@field preference? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocationPreferenceEnum|string Preference for a given location. Set to either ALLOW orDENY.
---@field names? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Names of resources to be put in the location. Must contain unique, correct resource names. If used, targetShape must be left unset.
---@field constraints? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocationConstraints Constraints that the caller requires on the result distribution in this zone.

---Per-zone constraints on location policy for this zone.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocationConstraints
---@field maxCount? number Maximum number of items that are allowed to be placed in this zone. The value must be non-negative.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocationMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocation }

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyLocationPreferenceEnum "ALLOW"|"DENY"|"PREFERENCE_UNSPECIFIED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyTargetShapeEnum "ANY"|"ANY_SINGLE_ZONE"|"BALANCED"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyZoneConfiguration
---@field zone? string The URL of the zone. The zone must exist in the region where the request is called. Zones must be represented as valid partial URLs, such as zones/us-central1-a.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyZoneConfigurationList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.LocationPolicyZoneConfiguration[]

---Represents a machine image resource.
---
---A machine image is a Compute Engine resource that stores all the
---configuration, metadata, permissions, and data from one or more disks
---required to create a Virtual machine (VM) instance. For more information, seeMachine images.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.MachineImage
---@field savedDisks? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SavedDiskList Output only. An array of Machine Image specific properties for disks attached to the source instance
---@field satisfiesPzi? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field sourceInstanceProperties? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SourceInstanceProperties Output only. [Output Only] DEPRECATED: Please use instance_properties instead for source instance related properties. New properties will not be added to this field.
