---Represents a traffic classification rule that describes one or more match
---conditions along with the action to be taken when traffic matches this
---condition.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRule
---@field targetServiceAccounts? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of service accounts indicating the sets of instances that are applied with this rule.
---@field priority? number An integer indicating the priority of a rule in the list. The priority must be a positive value between 1 and 2147482647. The priority values from 2147482648 to 2147483647 (1000) are reserved for system default network policy rules. Rules are evaluated from highest to lowest priority where 1 is the highest priority and 2147483647 is the lowest priority.
---@field targetSecureTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleSecureTagList A list of secure tags that controls which instances the traffic classification rule applies to. If targetSecureTag are specified, then the traffic classification rule applies only to instances in the VPC network that have one of those EFFECTIVE secure tags, if all the targetSecureTag are in INEFFECTIVE state, then this rule will be ignored. targetSecureTag may not be set at the same time as targetServiceAccounts. If neithertargetServiceAccounts nor targetSecureTag are specified, the traffic classification rule applies to all instances on the specified network. Maximum number of target label tags allowed is 256.
---@field action? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleAction The Action to perform when the client connection triggers the rule.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#networkPolicyTrafficClassificationRule for network policy traffic classification rules
---@field disabled? boolean Denotes whether the network policy rule is disabled. When set to true, the network policy rule is not enforced and traffic behaves as if it did not exist. If this is unspecified, the network policy rule will be enabled.
---@field ruleName? string An optional name for the rule. This field is not a unique identifier and can be updated.
---@field description? string An optional description for this resource.
---@field ruleTupleCount? number Output only. [Output Only] Calculation of the complexity of a single network policy rule.
---@field match? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleMatcher A match condition that outgoing traffic is evaluated against. If it evaluates to true, the corresponding 'action' is enforced.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleAction
---@field dscpValue? number Custom DSCP value from 0-63 range.
---@field type? string Always "apply_traffic_classification" for traffic classification rules.
---@field trafficClass? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleActionTrafficClassEnum|string The traffic class that should be applied to the matching packet.
---@field dscpMode? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleActionDscpModeEnum|string DSCP mode. When set to AUTO, the DSCP value will be picked automatically based on selected trafficClass. Otherwise,dscpValue needs to be explicitly specified.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleActionDscpModeEnum "AUTO"|"CUSTOM"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleActionTrafficClassEnum "TC1"|"TC2"|"TC3"|"TC4"|"TC5"|"TC6"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRule[]

---Represents a match condition that incoming traffic is evaluated against.
---Exactly one field must be specified.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleMatcher
---@field destAddressGroups? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Address groups which should be matched against the traffic destination. Maximum number of destination address groups is 10. Example: projects//locations//addressGroups/.
---@field layer4Configs? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleMatcherLayer4ConfigList Pairs of IP protocols and ports that the rule should match.
---@field destIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList CIDR IP address range. Maximum number of destination CIDR IP ranges allowed is 5000.
---@field srcIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList CIDR IP address range. Maximum number of source CIDR IP ranges allowed is 5000.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleMatcherLayer4Config
---@field ports? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList An optional list of ports to which this rule applies. This field is only applicable for UDP, TCP or SCTP protocol. Each entry must be either an integer or a range. If not specified, this rule applies to connections through any port. Example inputs include: ["22"],["80","443"], and ["12345-12349"].
---@field ipProtocol? string The IP protocol to which this rule applies. The protocol type is required when creating a traffic classification rule. This value can either be one of the following well known protocol strings (tcp, udp, icmp,esp, ah, ipip,sctp), or the IP protocol number.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleMatcherLayer4ConfigList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleMatcherLayer4Config[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleSecureTag
---@field name? string Name of the secure tag, created with TagManager's TagValue API.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleSecureTagStateEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] State of the secure tag, either `EFFECTIVE` or `INEFFECTIVE`. A secure tag is `INEFFECTIVE` when it is deleted or its network is deleted.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleSecureTagList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleSecureTag[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NetworkPolicyTrafficClassificationRuleSecureTagStateEnum "EFFECTIVE"|"INEFFECTIVE"|"STATE_UNSPECIFIED"

