---Represents a sole-tenant Node Group resource.
---
---A sole-tenant node is a physical server that is dedicated to
---hosting VM instances only for your specific project. Use sole-tenant nodes to
---keep your instances physically separated from instances in other projects, or
---to group your instances together on the same host hardware. For more
---information, readSole-tenant nodes.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NodeGroup
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] The type of the resource. Alwayscompute#nodeGroup for node group.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field zone? string Output only. [Output Only] The name of the zone where the node group resides, such as us-central1-a.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field maintenanceInterval? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NodeGroupMaintenanceIntervalEnum Specifies the frequency of planned maintenance events. The accepted values are: `AS_NEEDED` and `RECURRENT`.
---@field nodeTemplate? string URL of the node template to create the node group from.
---@field size? number Output only. [Output Only] The total number of nodes in the node group.
---@field maintenanceWindow? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NodeGroupMaintenanceWindow
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NodeGroupStatusEnum
---@field maintenancePolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NodeGroupMaintenancePolicyEnum Specifies how to handle instances when a node in the group undergoes maintenance. Set to one of: DEFAULT,RESTART_IN_PLACE, or MIGRATE_WITHIN_NODE_GROUP. The default value is DEFAULT. For more information, see Maintenance policies.
---@field shareSettings? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShareSettings Share-settings for the node group
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field fingerprint? string
---@field locationHint? string An opaque location hint used to place the Node close to other resources. This field is for use by internal tools that use the public API. The location hint here on the NodeGroup overrides any location_hint present in the NodeTemplate.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field autoscalingPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.NodeGroupAutoscalingPolicy Specifies how autoscaling should behave.
---@field name? string The name of the resource, provided by the client when initially creating the resource. The resource name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.

