---Represents a Packet Mirroring resource.
---
---Packet Mirroring clones the traffic of specified instances in your Virtual
---Private Cloud (VPC) network and forwards it to a collector destination,
---such as an instance group of an internal TCP/UDP load balancer, for analysis
---or examination.
---For more information about setting up Packet Mirroring, seeUsing Packet Mirroring.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.PacketMirroring
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#packetMirroring for packet mirrorings.
---@field region? string [Output Only] URI of the region where the packetMirroring resides.
---@field network? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.PacketMirroringNetworkInfo Specifies the mirrored VPC network. Only packets in this network will be mirrored. All mirrored VMs should have a NIC in the given network. All mirrored subnetworks should belong to the given network.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field priority? number The priority of applying this configuration. Priority is used to break ties in cases where there is more than one matching rule. In the case of two rules that apply for a given Instance, the one with the lowest-numbered priority value wins. Default value is 1000. Valid range is 0 through 65535.
---@field mirroredResources? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.PacketMirroringMirroredResourceInfo PacketMirroring mirroredResourceInfos. MirroredResourceInfo specifies a set of mirrored VM instances, subnetworks and/or tags for which traffic from/to all VM instances will be mirrored.
---@field filter? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.PacketMirroringFilter Filter for mirrored traffic. If unspecified, all IPv4 traffic is mirrored.
---@field name? string Name of the resource; provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field enable? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.PacketMirroringEnableEnum Indicates whether or not this packet mirroring takes effect. If set to FALSE, this packet mirroring policy will not be enforced on the network. The default is TRUE.
---@field collectorIlb? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.PacketMirroringForwardingRuleInfo The Forwarding Rule resource of typeloadBalancingScheme=INTERNAL that will be used as collector for mirrored traffic. The specified forwarding rule must have isMirroringCollector set to true.

