---@field cloudArmorTier? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ProjectCloudArmorTierEnum Output only. [Output Only] The Cloud Armor tier for this project. It can be one of the following values: CA_STANDARD,CA_ENTERPRISE_PAYGO. If this field is not specified, it is assumed to beCA_STANDARD.
---@field creationTimestamp? string [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field name? string The project ID. For example: my-example-project. Use the project ID to make requests to Compute Engine.
---@field vmDnsSetting? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ProjectVmDnsSettingEnum Output only. [Output Only] Default internal DNS setting used by VMs running in this project.
---@field defaultServiceAccount? string [Output Only] Default service account used by VMs running in this project.
---@field quotas? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.QuotaList [Output Only] Quotas assigned to this project.
---@field usageExportLocation? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UsageExportLocation An optional naming prefix for daily usage reports and the Google Cloud Storage bucket where they are stored.
---@field managedProtectionTier? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ProjectManagedProtectionTierEnum Output only. [Output Only] The Cloud Armor Managed Protection (CAMP) tier for this project. It can be one of the following values:CA_STANDARD, CAMP_PLUS_PAYGO. If this field is not specified, it is assumed to beCA_STANDARD.
---@field enabledFeatures? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList An optional list of restricted features enabled for use on this project.
---@field id? string [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server. This is *not* the project ID, and is just a unique ID used by Compute Engine to identify resources.
---@field description? string An optional textual description of the resource.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Always compute#project for projects.
---@field selfLink? string [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field commonInstanceMetadata? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Metadata Metadata key/value pairs available to all instances contained in this project. See Custom metadata for more information.
---@field defaultNetworkTier? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ProjectDefaultNetworkTierEnum This signifies the default network tier used for configuring resources of the project and can only take the following values:PREMIUM, STANDARD. Initially the default network tier is PREMIUM.

