---A policy that specifies how requests intended for the route's backends
---are shadowed to a separate mirrored backend service. The load balancer
---doesn't wait for responses from the shadow service. Before sending traffic
---to the shadow service, the host or authority header is suffixed with-shadow.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RequestMirrorPolicy
---@field mirrorPercent? number The percentage of requests to be mirrored to `backend_service`.
---@field backendService? string The full or partial URL to the BackendService resource being mirrored to. The backend service configured for a mirroring policy must reference backends that are of the same type as the original backend service matched in the URL map. Serverless NEG backends are not currently supported as a mirrored backend service.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RequestRemovePeeringNetworksRequest
---@field name? string Name of the peering, which should conform to RFC1035.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field network string Name of the network resource to remove peering from.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.

---Represents a reservation resource.  A reservation ensures that capacity is
---held in a specific zone even if the reserved VMs are not running. For more
---information, read  Reserving zonal
---resources.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Reservation
---@field specificReservation? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationSpecificSKUReservation Reservation for instances with specific machine shapes.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Reserved for future use.
---@field advancedDeploymentControl? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAdvancedDeploymentControl Advanced control for cluster management, applicable only to DENSE deployment type reservations.
---@field shareSettings? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShareSettings Specify share-settings to create a shared reservation. This property is optional. For more information about the syntax and options for this field and its subfields, see the guide for creating a shared reservation.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined fully-qualified URL for this resource.
---@field deploymentType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationDeploymentTypeEnum|string Specifies the deployment strategy for this reservation.
---@field protectionTier? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationProtectionTierEnum|string Protection tier for the workload which specifies the workload expectations in the event of infrastructure failures at data center (e.g. power and/or cooling failures).
---@field deleteAtTime? string Absolute time in future when the reservation will be auto-deleted by Compute Engine. Timestamp is represented inRFC3339 text format.
---@field reservationSharingPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationReservationSharingPolicy Specify the reservation sharing policy. If unspecified, the reservation will not be shared with Google Cloud managed services.
---@field confidentialComputeType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationConfidentialComputeTypeEnum|string
---@field zone? string Zone in which the reservation resides. A zone must be provided if the reservation is created within a commitment.
---@field resourceStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationResourceStatus Output only. [Output Only] Status information for Reservation resource.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field resourcePolicies? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap Resource policies to be added to this reservation. The key is defined by user, and the value is resource policy url. This is to define placement policy with reservation.
---@field enableEmergentMaintenance? boolean Indicates whether Compute Engine allows unplanned maintenance for your VMs; for example, to fix hardware errors.
---@field commitment? string Output only. [Output Only] Full or partial URL to a parent commitment. This field displays for reservations that are tied to a commitment.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field name? string The name of the resource, provided by the client when initially creating the resource. The resource name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field deleteAfterDuration? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Duration Duration time relative to reservation creation when Compute Engine will automatically delete this resource.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Alwayscompute#reservations for reservations.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field schedulingType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationSchedulingTypeEnum|string The type of maintenance for the reservation.
---@field aggregateReservation? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AllocationAggregateReservation Reservation for aggregated resources, providing shape flexibility.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationStatusEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] The status of the reservation. - CREATING: Reservation resources are being allocated. - READY: Reservation resources have been allocated, and the reservation is ready for use. - DELETING: Reservation deletion is in progress. - UPDATING: Reservation update is in progress.
---@field reservationMode? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationReservationModeEnum|string Output only. [Output only] Indicates the reservation mode of the reservation.
---@field linkedCommitments? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. [Output Only] Full or partial URL to parent commitments. This field displays for reservations that are tied to multiple commitments.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationParams Input only. Additional params passed with the request, but not persisted as part of resource payload.
---@field specificReservationRequired? boolean Indicates whether the reservation can be consumed by VMs with affinity for "any" reservation. If the field is set, then only VMs that target the reservation by name can consume from this reservation.
---@field earlyAccessMaintenance? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationEarlyAccessMaintenanceEnum|string Indicates the early access maintenance for the reservation. If this field is absent or set to NO_EARLY_ACCESS, the reservation is not enrolled in early access maintenance and the standard notice applies.

---Advance control for cluster management, applicable only to DENSE deployment
---type reservations.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAdvancedDeploymentControl
---@field reservationOperationalMode? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAdvancedDeploymentControlReservationOperationalModeEnum|string Indicates chosen reservation operational mode for the reservation.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAdvancedDeploymentControlReservationOperationalModeEnum "ALL_CAPACITY"|"HIGHLY_AVAILABLE_CAPACITY"|"RESERVATION_OPERATIONAL_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"

---Specifies the reservations that this instance can consume from.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAffinity
---@field values? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Corresponds to the label values of a reservation resource. This can be either a name to a reservation in the same project or "projects/different-project/reservations/some-reservation-name" to target a shared reservation in the same zone but in a different project.
---@field key? string Corresponds to the label key of a reservation resource. To target aSPECIFIC_RESERVATION by name, specifygoogleapis.com/reservation-name as the key and specify the name of your reservation as its value.
---@field consumeReservationType? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAffinityConsumeReservationTypeEnum|string Specifies the type of reservation from which this instance can consume resources: ANY_RESERVATION (default),SPECIFIC_RESERVATION, or NO_RESERVATION. See Consuming reserved instances for examples.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ReservationAffinityConsumeReservationTypeEnum "ANY_RESERVATION"|"ANY_RESERVATION_THEN_FAIL"|"NO_RESERVATION"|"SPECIFIC_RESERVATION"|"SPECIFIC_THEN_ANY_RESERVATION"|"SPECIFIC_THEN_NO_RESERVATION"|"UNSPECIFIED"

