---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ResumeInstancesInstanceGroupManagersRequest
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList The URLs of one or more instances to resume. This can be a full URL or a partial URL, such as zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME].
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field zone string The name of thezone where the managed instance group is located.
---@field instanceGroupManager string The name of the managed instance group.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ResumeInstancesRegionInstanceGroupManagersRequest
---@field instances? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList The URLs of one or more instances to resume. This can be a full URL or a partial URL, such as zones/[ZONE]/instances/[INSTANCE_NAME].
---@field region string Name of the region scoping this request.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.
---@field instanceGroupManager string Name of the managed instance group.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ResumeInstancesRequest
---@field disks? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CustomerEncryptionKeyProtectedDiskList Array of disks associated with this instance that are protected with acustomer-supplied encryption key. In order to resume the instance, the disk url and its corresponding key must be provided. If the disk is not protected with a customer-supplied encryption key it should not be specified.
---@field instanceEncryptionKey? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.CustomerEncryptionKey Decrypts data associated with an instance that is protected with acustomer-supplied encryption key. If the instance you are starting is protected with a customer-supplied encryption key, the correct key must be provided otherwise the instance resume will not succeed.
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field zone string The name of the zone for this request.
---@field instance string Name of the instance resource to resume.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ResumeOrganizationRolloutsRequest
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field etag? string The etag of the Rollout. If this is provided, the request will only succeed if the etag matches the current etag of the Rollout.
---@field rollout string Required. Name of the Rollout resource to resume.
---@field organization string Required. Organization ID for this request.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ResumeRolloutsRequest
---@field requestId? string An optional request ID to identify requests. Specify a unique request ID so that if you must retry your request, the server will know to ignore the request if it has already been completed. For example, consider a situation where you make an initial request and the request times out. If you make the request again with the same request ID, the server can check if original operation with the same request ID was received, and if so, will ignore the second request. This prevents clients from accidentally creating duplicate commitments. The request ID must be a valid UUID with the exception that zero UUID is not supported (00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000).
---@field project string Required. Project ID for this request.
---@field etag? string The etag of the Rollout. If this is provided, the request will only succeed if the etag matches the current etag of the Rollout.
---@field rollout string Required. Name of the Rollout resource to resume.

