---Rollout resource.
---
---A Rollout is a specific instance of a RolloutPlan. It represents a single
---execution of a strategy to roll out a specific resource. It also provides
---APIs to interact with the rollout.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Rollout
---@field rolloutPlan? string Required. Rollout Plan used to model the Rollout. Ex. compute.googleapis.com/v1/projects/1234/rolloutPlans/rp1
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Always compute#rollout for rollouts.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined fully-qualified URL for this resource.
---@field rolloutEntity? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutRolloutEntity Required. The resource being rolled out.
---@field resumeTime? string Output only. The timestamp at which the Rollout was resumed.
---@field waveDetails? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutWaveDetailsList Output only. Details about each wave of the rollout.
---@field etag? string Output only. etag of the Rollout Ex. abc1234
---@field cancellationTime? string Output only. The timestamp at which the Rollout was cancelled.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource's resource id.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutStateEnum Output only. The current state of the Rollout.
---@field currentWaveNumber? string Output only. The number of the currently running wave. Ex. 1
---@field pauseTime? string Output only. The timestamp at which the Rollout was paused.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field completionTime? string Output only. The timestamp at which the Rollout was completed.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Rollout[]

---RolloutPlan resource.
---
---A RolloutPlan is the customer-defined strategy to divide a large-scale change
---into smaller increments, referred to as "waves". Each wave targets a specific
---portion of the overall affected area and defines criteria that must be met
---before progressing to the subsequent wave.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlan
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource's resource id.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field locationScope? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanLocationScopeEnum The location scope of the rollout plan. If not specified, the location scope is considered as ZONAL.
---@field waves? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveList Required. The waves included in this rollout plan.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of the resource. Always compute#rolloutPlan for rolloutPlans.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined fully-qualified URL for this resource.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlan[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanLocationScopeEnum "LOCATION_SCOPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"REGIONAL"|"ZONAL"

---A single wave in a rollout plan.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWave
---@field orchestrationOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptions Optional. The orchestration options for this wave.
---@field validation? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveValidation Required. The validation to be performed at the end of this wave.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of this wave of the rollout plan.
---@field selectors? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelectorList Required. The selectors for this wave. There is a logical AND between each selector defined in a wave, so a resource must satisfy the criteria of *all* the specified selectors to be in scope for the wave.
---@field number? string Output only. The wave number.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWave[]

---Options to control the pace of orchestration of a wave. These options are
---required only if the resource being rolled out follows the Orchestrated
---pattern.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptions
---@field maxConcurrentResourcesPerLocation? string Optional. Maximum number of resources to be orchestrated per location in parallel.
---@field maxConcurrentLocations? string Optional. Maximum number of locations to be orchestrated in parallel.
---@field delays? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelayList Optional. Delays, if any, to be added between batches of projects. We allow multiple Delays to be specified, letting users set separate delays between batches of projects corresponding to different locations and batches of projects corresponding to the same location.

---Options to control the delay, if any, between batches of projects.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelay
---@field delimiter? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelayDelimiterEnum|string Optional. Controls whether the delay should only be added between batches of projects corresponding to different locations, or also between batches of projects corresponding to the same location. Must be set to DELIMITER_UNSPECIFIED if no delay is to be added.
---@field duration? string Optional. The duration of the delay, if any, to be added between batches of projects. A zero duration corresponds to no delay.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelayTypeEnum|string Optional. Controls whether the specified duration is to be added at the end of each batch, or if the total processing time for each batch will be padded if needed to meet the specified duration. Must be set to TYPE_UNSPECIFIED if no delay is to be added.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelayDelimiterEnum "DELIMITER_BATCH"|"DELIMITER_LOCATION"|"DELIMITER_UNSPECIFIED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelayList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelay[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveOrchestrationOptionsDelayTypeEnum "TYPE_MINIMUM"|"TYPE_OFFSET"|"TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"

---A selector which specifies what resource(s) are included in a given wave.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelector
---@field resourceHierarchySelector? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelectorResourceHierarchySelector Optional. Roll out to resources by Cloud Resource Manager resource hierarchy.
---@field locationSelector? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelectorLocationSelector Optional. Roll out to resources by Cloud locations.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelectorList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelector[]

---Roll out to resources by location.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelectorLocationSelector
---@field includedLocations? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Optional. Example: "us-central1-a"

---Roll out to resources by Cloud Resource Manager resource hierarchy
---nodes such as projects, folders, orgs.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveSelectorResourceHierarchySelector
---@field includedFolders? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Optional. Format: "folders/{folder_id}"
---@field includedProjects? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Optional. Format: "projects/{project_id}"
---@field includedOrganizations? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Optional. Format: "organizations/{organization_id}"

---The validation to be performed before progressing to the next wave.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveValidation
---@field type? string Required. The type of the validation. If a type of validation is associated with a metadata object, the appropriate metadata field mapping to the validation type must be provided in the validation message. Possible values are in quotes below alongside an explanation: "manual": The system waits for an end-user approval API before progressing to the next wave. "time": The system waits for a user specified duration before progressing to the next wave. TimeBasedValidation must be provided.
---@field timeBasedValidationMetadata? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveValidationTimeBasedValidationMetadata Optional. Metadata required if type = "time".

---Metadata required if type = "time".
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RolloutPlanWaveValidationTimeBasedValidationMetadata
