---Represents a Cloud Router resource.
---
---For more information about Cloud Router, read theCloud
---Router overview.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Router
---@field interfaces? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterInterfaceList Router interfaces. To create a BGP peer that uses a router interface, the interface must have one of the following fields specified: - linkedVpnTunnel - linkedInterconnectAttachment - subnetwork You can create a router interface without any of these fields specified. However, you cannot create a BGP peer that uses that interface.
---@field name? string Name of the resource. Provided by the client when the resource is created. The name must be 1-63 characters long, and comply withRFC1035. Specifically, the name must be 1-63 characters long and match the regular expression `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?` which means the first character must be a lowercase letter, and all following characters must be a dash, lowercase letter, or digit, except the last character, which cannot be a dash.
---@field bgp? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterBgp BGP information specific to this router.
---@field nccGateway? string URI of the ncc_gateway to which this router associated.
---@field region? string [Output Only] URI of the region where the router resides. You must specify this field as part of the HTTP request URL. It is not settable as a field in the request body.
---@field creationTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Creation timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field id? string [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field etag? string ETag for optimistic concurrency control as described by AIP 154. Used to prevent conflicting updates. If provided, the request will succeed only if the etag matches the current etag of the router; otherwise, the request fails with an ABORTED error.
---@field nats? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatList A list of NAT services created in this router.
---@field selfLinkWithId? string Output only. [Output Only] Server-defined URL for this resource with the resource id.
---@field bgpPeers? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterBgpPeerList BGP information that must be configured into the routing stack to establish BGP peering. This information must specify the peer ASN and either the interface name, IP address, or peer IP address. Please refer toRFC4273.
---@field network? string URI of the network to which this router belongs.
---@field selfLink? string [Output Only] Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field md5AuthenticationKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterMd5AuthenticationKeyList Keys used for MD5 authentication.
---@field params? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterParams Input only. [Input Only] Additional params passed with the request, but not persisted as part of resource payload.
---@field kind? string Output only. [Output Only] Type of resource. Always compute#router for routers.
---@field description? string An optional description of this resource. Provide this property when you create the resource.
---@field encryptedInterconnectRouter? boolean Indicates if a router is dedicated for use with encrypted VLAN attachments (interconnectAttachments).

