---Represents a Nat resource. It enables the VMs within the specified
---subnetworks to access Internet without external IP addresses. It specifies
---a list of subnetworks (and the ranges within) that want to use NAT.
---Customers can also provide the external IPs that would be used for NAT. GCP
---would auto-allocate ephemeral IPs if no external IPs are provided.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNat
---@field subnetworks? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatList A list of Subnetwork resources whose traffic should be translated by NAT Gateway. It is used only when LIST_OF_SUBNETWORKS is selected for the SubnetworkIpRangeToNatOption above.
---@field minPortsPerVm? number Minimum number of ports allocated to a VM from this NAT config. If not set, a default number of ports is allocated to a VM. This is rounded up to the nearest power of 2. For example, if the value of this field is 50, at least 64 ports are allocated to a VM.
---@field udpIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for UDP connections. Defaults to 30s if not set.
---@field endpointTypes? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnumList List of NAT-ted endpoint types supported by the Nat Gateway. If the list is empty, then it will be equivalent to include ENDPOINT_TYPE_VM
---@field icmpIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for ICMP connections. Defaults to 30s if not set.
---@field sourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat64? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat64Enum|string Specify the Nat option for NAT64, which can take one of the following values: - ALL_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS: All of the IP ranges in every Subnetwork are allowed to Nat. - LIST_OF_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS: A list of Subnetworks are allowed to Nat (specified in the field nat64_subnetwork below) The default is NAT64_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED. Note that if this field contains NAT64_ALL_V6_SUBNETWORKS no other Router.Nat section in this region can also enable NAT64 for any Subnetworks in this network. Other Router.Nat sections can still be present to enable NAT44 only.
---@field name? string Unique name of this Nat service. The name must be 1-63 characters long and comply withRFC1035.
---@field autoNetworkTier? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatAutoNetworkTierEnum|string The network tier to use when automatically reserving NAT IP addresses. Must be one of: PREMIUM, STANDARD. If not specified, then the current project-level default tier is used.
---@field tcpTransitoryIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for TCP transitory connections. Defaults to 30s if not set.
---@field natIpAllocateOption? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatNatIpAllocateOptionEnum|string Specify the NatIpAllocateOption, which can take one of the following values: - MANUAL_ONLY: Uses only Nat IP addresses provided by customers. When there are not enough specified Nat IPs, the Nat service fails for new VMs. - AUTO_ONLY: Nat IPs are allocated by Google Cloud Platform; customers can't specify any Nat IPs. When choosing AUTO_ONLY, then nat_ip should be empty.
---@field natIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources used for this Nat service. These IP addresses must be valid static external IP addresses assigned to the project.
---@field nat64Subnetworks? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64List List of Subnetwork resources whose traffic should be translated by NAT64 Gateway. It is used only when LIST_OF_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS is selected for the SubnetworkIpRangeToNat64Option above.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatTypeEnum|string Indicates whether this NAT is used for public or private IP translation. If unspecified, it defaults to PUBLIC.
---@field rules? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatRuleList A list of rules associated with this NAT.
---@field sourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNatEnum|string Specify the Nat option, which can take one of the following values: - ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_IP_RANGES: All of the IP ranges in every Subnetwork are allowed to Nat. - ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_PRIMARY_IP_RANGES: All of the primary IP ranges in every Subnetwork are allowed to Nat. - LIST_OF_SUBNETWORKS: A list of Subnetworks are allowed to Nat (specified in the field subnetwork below) The default is SUBNETWORK_IP_RANGE_TO_NAT_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED. Note that if this field contains ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_IP_RANGES then there should not be any other Router.Nat section in any Router for this network in this region.
---@field enableDynamicPortAllocation? boolean Enable Dynamic Port Allocation. If not specified, it is disabled by default. If set to true, - Dynamic Port Allocation will be enabled on this NAT config. - enableEndpointIndependentMapping cannot be set to true. - If minPorts is set, minPortsPerVm must be set to a power of two greater than or equal to 32. If minPortsPerVm is not set, a minimum of 32 ports will be allocated to a VM from this NAT config.
---@field tcpEstablishedIdleTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for TCP established connections. Defaults to 1200s if not set.
---@field drainNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources to be drained. These IPs must be valid static external IPs that have been assigned to the NAT. These IPs should be used for updating/patching a NAT only.
---@field maxPortsPerVm? number Maximum number of ports allocated to a VM from this NAT config when Dynamic Port Allocation is enabled. If Dynamic Port Allocation is not enabled, this field has no effect. If Dynamic Port Allocation is enabled, and this field is set, it must be set to a power of two greater than minPortsPerVm, or 64 if minPortsPerVm is not set. If Dynamic Port Allocation is enabled and this field is not set, a maximum of 65536 ports will be allocated to a VM from this NAT config.
---@field tcpTimeWaitTimeoutSec? number Timeout (in seconds) for TCP connections that are in TIME_WAIT state. Defaults to 120s if not set.
---@field logConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatLogConfig Configure logging on this NAT.
---@field enableEndpointIndependentMapping? boolean
---@field effectiveTcpTimeWaitTimeoutSec? number Output only. Effective timeout (in seconds) for TCP connections that are in TIME_WAIT state. This value is equal to tcp_time_wait_timeout_sec. If tcp_time_wait_timeout_sec isn't set, the effective timeout is 30s or 120s. The field is output only.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatAutoNetworkTierEnum "FIXED_STANDARD"|"PREMIUM"|"SELECT"|"STANDARD"|"STANDARD_OVERRIDES_FIXED_STANDARD"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnum "ENDPOINT_TYPE_MANAGED_PROXY_LB"|"ENDPOINT_TYPE_SWG"|"ENDPOINT_TYPE_VM"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatEndpointTypesItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNat[]

---Configuration of logging on a NAT.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatLogConfig
---@field enable? boolean Indicates whether or not to export logs. This is false by default.
---@field filter? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatLogConfigFilterEnum|string Specify the desired filtering of logs on this NAT. If unspecified, logs are exported for all connections handled by this NAT. This option can take one of the following values: - ERRORS_ONLY: Export logs only for connection failures. - TRANSLATIONS_ONLY: Export logs only for successful connections. - ALL: Export logs for all connections, successful and unsuccessful.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatLogConfigFilterEnum "ALL"|"ERRORS_ONLY"|"TRANSLATIONS_ONLY"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatNatIpAllocateOptionEnum "AUTO_ONLY"|"MANUAL_ONLY"

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatRule
---@field action? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatRuleAction The action to be enforced for traffic that matches this rule.
---@field match? string CEL expression that specifies the match condition that egress traffic from a VM is evaluated against. If it evaluates to true, the corresponding `action` is enforced. The following examples are valid match expressions for public NAT: `inIpRange(destination.ip, '1.1.0.0/16') || inIpRange(destination.ip, '2.2.0.0/16')` `destination.ip == '1.1.0.1' || destination.ip == '8.8.8.8'` The following examples are valid match expressions for private NAT: (NAT 44) `nexthop.hub == '//networkconnectivity.googleapis.com/projects/my-project/locations/global/hubs/hub-1'` `nexthop.is_hybrid` (NAT 64) `isIPv6(source.ip)`
---@field description? string An optional description of this rule.
---@field sourceWorkloadIdentities? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of source workload identities.
---@field ruleNumber? number An integer uniquely identifying a rule in the list. The rule number must be a positive value between 0 and 65000, and must be unique among rules within a NAT.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatRuleAction
---@field sourceNatDrainIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources to be drained. These IPs must be valid static external IPs that have been assigned to the NAT. These IPs should be used for updating/patching a NAT rule only. This field is used for public NAT.
---@field sourceNatDrainRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of URLs of subnetworks representing source ranges to be drained. This is only supported on patch/update, and these subnetworks must have previously been used as active ranges in this NAT Rule. This field is used for private NAT.
---@field sourceNatActiveRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of URLs of the subnetworks used as source ranges for this NAT Rule. These subnetworks must have purpose set to PRIVATE_NAT. This field is used for private NAT.
---@field sourceNatActiveIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of URLs of the IP resources used for this NAT rule. These IP addresses must be valid static external IP addresses assigned to the project. This field is used for public NAT.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatRuleList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatRule[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNat64Enum "ALL_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS"|"LIST_OF_IPV6_SUBNETWORKS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSourceSubnetworkIpRangesToNatEnum "ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_IP_RANGES"|"ALL_SUBNETWORKS_ALL_PRIMARY_IP_RANGES"|"LIST_OF_SUBNETWORKS"

---Defines the IP ranges that want to use NAT for a subnetwork.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat
---@field secondaryIpRangeNames? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of the secondary ranges of the Subnetwork that are allowed to use NAT. This can be populated only if "LIST_OF_SECONDARY_IP_RANGES" is one of the values in source_ip_ranges_to_nat.
---@field name? string URL for the subnetwork resource that will use NAT.
---@field sourceIpRangesToNat? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnumList Specify the options for NAT ranges in the Subnetwork. All options of a single value are valid except NAT_IP_RANGE_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED. The only valid option with multiple values is: ["PRIMARY_IP_RANGE", "LIST_OF_SECONDARY_IP_RANGES"] Default: [ALL_IP_RANGES]

---Specifies a subnetwork to enable NAT64.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64
---@field name? string URL for the subnetwork resource that will use NAT64.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64List gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat64[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNat[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnum "ALL_IP_RANGES"|"LIST_OF_SECONDARY_IP_RANGES"|"PRIMARY_IP_RANGE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatSubnetworkToNatSourceIpRangesToNatItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterNatTypeEnum "PRIVATE"|"PUBLIC"

---Additional router parameters.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterParams
---@field resourceManagerTags? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringMap Tag keys/values directly bound to this resource. The field is allowed for INSERT only. The keys/values to set on the resource should be specified in either ID { : } or Namespaced format { : }. For example the following are valid inputs: * {"tagKeys/333" : "tagValues/444", "tagKeys/123" : "tagValues/456"} * {"123/environment" : "production", "345/abc" : "xyz"} Note: * Invalid combinations of ID & namespaced format is not supported. For instance: {"123/environment" : "tagValues/444"} is invalid. * Inconsistent format is not supported. For instance: {"tagKeys/333" : "tagValues/444", "123/env" : "prod"} is invalid.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatus
---@field network? string URI of the network to which this router belongs.
---@field bgpPeerStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusList
---@field bestRoutesForRouter? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouteList_ A list of the best BGP routes learned by this Cloud Router. It is possible that routes listed might not be programmed into the data plane, if the Google Cloud control plane finds a more optimal route for a prefix than a route learned by this Cloud Router.
---@field natStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatusList
---@field bestRoutes? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouteList_ A list of the best dynamic routes for this Cloud Router's Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) network in the same region as this Cloud Router. Lists all of the best routes per prefix that are programmed into this region's VPC data plane. When global dynamic routing mode is turned on in the VPC network, this list can include cross-region dynamic routes from Cloud Routers in other regions.
---@field nccGateway? string URI of the ncc_gateway to which this router associated.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatus
---@field uptime? string Output only. Time this session has been up. Format: 14 years, 51 weeks, 6 days, 23 hours, 59 minutes, 59 seconds
---@field depreferenced? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Indicates whether the BGP peer is in a depreferenced state.
---@field ipv4NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv4 address of the local BGP interface.
---@field peerIpAddress? string Output only. IP address of the remote BGP interface.
---@field md5AuthEnabled? boolean Informs whether MD5 authentication is enabled on this BGP peer.
---@field enableIpv6? boolean Output only. Enable IPv6 traffic over BGP Peer. It is enabled by default if the peerIpAddress is version 6.
---@field peerIpv4NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv4 address of the remote BGP interface.
---@field name? string Output only. Name of this BGP peer. Unique within the Routers resource.
---@field uptimeSeconds? string Output only. Time this session has been up, in seconds. Format: 145
---@field routerApplianceInstance? string Output only. [Output only] URI of the VM instance that is used as third-party router appliances such as Next Gen Firewalls, Virtual Routers, or Router Appliances. The VM instance is the peer side of the BGP session.
---@field linkedCustomHardware? string Output only. The URI of the linked custom hardware resource, CustomHardwareLinkAttachment. This CustomHardwareLinkAttachment resource is the one that will establish the BGP session from the Cloud Router.
---@field ipv6NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv6 address of the local BGP interface.
---@field statusReason? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusReasonEnum Indicates why particular status was returned.
---@field linkedVpnTunnel? string Output only. URL of the VPN tunnel that this BGP peer controls.
---@field state? string Output only. The state of the BGP session. For a list of possible values for this field, seeBGP session states.
---@field peerIpv6NexthopAddress? string Output only. IPv6 address of the remote BGP interface.
---@field advertisedRoutes? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouteList_ Routes that were advertised to the remote BGP peer
---@field enableIpv4? boolean Output only. Enable IPv4 traffic over BGP Peer. It is enabled by default if the peerIpAddress is version 4.
---@field bfdStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.BfdStatus
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusEnum Output only. Status of the BGP peer: {UP, DOWN}
---@field numLearnedRoutes? number Output only. Number of routes learned from the remote BGP Peer.
---@field ipAddress? string Output only. IP address of the local BGP interface.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatus[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusEnum "DOWN"|"UNKNOWN"|"UP"

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusBgpPeerStatusStatusReasonEnum "IPV4_PEER_ON_IPV6_ONLY_CONNECTION"|"IPV6_PEER_ON_IPV4_ONLY_CONNECTION"|"MD5_AUTH_INTERNAL_PROBLEM"|"STATUS_REASON_UNSPECIFIED"

---Status of a NAT contained in this router.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatus
---@field userAllocatedNatIpResources? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. A list of fully qualified URLs of reserved IP address resources.
---@field drainUserAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. A list of IPs user-allocated for NAT that are in drain mode. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "179.12.26.133"].
---@field autoAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. A list of IPs auto-allocated for NAT. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "129.2.16.89"]
---@field name? string Output only. Unique name of this NAT.
---@field ruleStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatusNatRuleStatusList Status of rules in this NAT.
---@field minExtraNatIpsNeeded? number Output only. The number of extra IPs to allocate. This will be greater than 0 only if user-specified IPs are NOT enough to allow all configured VMs to use NAT. This value is meaningful only when auto-allocation of NAT IPs is *not* used.
---@field drainAutoAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. A list of IPs auto-allocated for NAT that are in drain mode. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "179.12.26.133"].
---@field numVmEndpointsWithNatMappings? number Output only. Number of VM endpoints (i.e., Nics) that can use NAT.
---@field userAllocatedNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. A list of IPs user-allocated for NAT. They will be raw IP strings like "179.12.26.133".

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatusList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatus[]

---Status of a NAT Rule contained in this NAT.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatusNatRuleStatus
---@field drainNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. A list of IPs for NAT that are in drain mode. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "179.12.26.133"].
---@field ruleNumber? number Output only. Rule number of the rule.
---@field activeNatIps? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Output only. A list of active IPs for NAT. Example: ["1.1.1.1", "179.12.26.133"].
---@field minExtraIpsNeeded? number Output only. The number of extra IPs to allocate. This will be greater than 0 only if the existing IPs in this NAT Rule are NOT enough to allow all configured VMs to use NAT.
---@field numVmEndpointsWithNatMappings? number Output only. Number of VM endpoints (i.e., NICs) that have NAT Mappings from this NAT Rule.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatusNatRuleStatusList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.RouterStatusNatStatusNatRuleStatus[]

