---Represents a match condition that incoming traffic is evaluated against.
---Exactly one field must be specified.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcher
---@field expr? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.Expr User defined CEVAL expression. A CEVAL expression is used to specify match criteria such as origin.ip, source.region_code and contents in the request header. Expressions containing `evaluateThreatIntelligence` require a Cloud Armor Enterprise subscription and are not supported in Edge Policies nor in Regional Policies. Expressions containing `evaluatePreconfiguredExpr('sourceiplist-*')` require a Cloud Armor Enterprise subscription and are only supported in Global Security Policies.
---@field exprOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptions The configuration options available when specifying a user defined CEVAL expression (i.e., 'expr').
---@field versionedExpr? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherVersionedExprEnum|string Preconfigured versioned expression. If this field is specified, config must also be specified. Available preconfigured expressions along with their requirements are: SRC_IPS_V1 - must specify the corresponding src_ip_range field in config.
---@field config? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfig The configuration options available when specifying versioned_expr. This field must be specified if versioned_expr is specified and cannot be specified if versioned_expr is not specified.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfig
---@field srcIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList CIDR IP address range. Maximum number of src_ip_ranges allowed is 10.
---@field layer4Configs? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4ConfigList Pairs of IP protocols and ports that the rule should match. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field destIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList CIDR IP address range. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field destPorts? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigDestinationPortList Pairs of IP protocols and ports that the rule should match. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigDestinationPort
---@field ipProtocol? string The IP protocol to which this rule applies. The protocol type is required when creating a firewall rule. This value can either be one of the following well known protocol strings (tcp,udp, icmp, esp,ah, ipip, sctp), or the IP protocol number.
---@field ports? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList An optional list of ports to which this rule applies. This field is only applicable for UDP or TCP protocol. Each entry must be either an integer or a range. If not specified, this rule applies to connections through any port. Example inputs include: ["22"],["80","443"], and ["12345-12349"]. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigDestinationPortList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigDestinationPort[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4Config
---@field ports? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList An optional list of ports to which this rule applies. This field is only applicable for UDP or TCP protocol. Each entry must be either an integer or a range. If not specified, this rule applies to connections through any port. Example inputs include: ["22"],["80","443"], and ["12345-12349"]. This field may only be specified when versioned_expr is set to FIREWALL.
---@field ipProtocol? string The IP protocol to which this rule applies. The protocol type is required when creating a firewall rule. This value can either be one of the following well known protocol strings (tcp,udp, icmp, esp,ah, ipip, sctp), or the IP protocol number.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4ConfigList gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherConfigLayer4Config[]

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptions
---@field recaptchaOptions? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptionsRecaptchaOptions reCAPTCHA configuration options to be applied for the rule. If the rule does not evaluate reCAPTCHA tokens, this field has no effect.

---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherExprOptionsRecaptchaOptions
---@field actionTokenSiteKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of site keys to be used during the validation of reCAPTCHA action-tokens. The provided site keys need to be created from reCAPTCHA API under the same project where the security policy is created.
---@field sessionTokenSiteKeys? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList A list of site keys to be used during the validation of reCAPTCHA session-tokens. The provided site keys need to be created from reCAPTCHA API under the same project where the security policy is created.

---@alias gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleMatcherVersionedExprEnum "FIREWALL"|"SRC_IPS_V1"

---Represents a match condition that incoming network traffic is evaluated
---against.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcher
---@field ipProtocols? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList IPv4 protocol / IPv6 next header (after extension headers). Each element can be an 8-bit unsigned decimal number (e.g. "6"), range (e.g. "253-254"), or one of the following protocol names: "tcp", "udp", "icmp", "esp", "ah", "ipip", or "sctp".
---@field userDefinedFields? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecurityPolicyRuleNetworkMatcherUserDefinedFieldMatchList User-defined fields. Each element names a defined field and lists the matching values for that field.
---@field srcPorts? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Source port numbers for TCP/UDP/SCTP. Each element can be a 16-bit unsigned decimal number (e.g. "80") or range (e.g. "0-1023").
---@field srcIpRanges? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Source IPv4/IPv6 addresses or CIDR prefixes, in standard text format.
