---The authentication and authorization settings for a BackendService.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.SecuritySettings
---@field awsV4Authentication? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AWSV4Signature The configuration needed to generate a signature for access to private storage buckets that support AWS's Signature Version 4 for authentication. Allowed only for INTERNET_IP_PORT and INTERNET_FQDN_PORT NEG backends.
---@field clientTlsPolicy? string Optional. A URL referring to a networksecurity.ClientTlsPolicy resource that describes how clients should authenticate with this service's backends. clientTlsPolicy only applies to a globalBackendService with the loadBalancingScheme set to INTERNAL_SELF_MANAGED. If left blank, communications are not encrypted.
---@field clientTlsSettings? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ClientTlsSettings [Deprecated] TLS Settings for the backend service.
---@field authentication? string [Deprecated] Use clientTlsPolicy instead.
---@field authorizationConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuthorizationConfig [Deprecated] Authorization config defines the Role Based Access Control (RBAC) config. Authorization config defines the Role Based Access Control (RBAC) config.
---@field authenticationPolicy? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AuthenticationPolicy [Deprecated] Authentication policy defines what authentication methods can be accepted on backends, and if authenticated, which method/certificate will set the request principal. request principal.
---@field subjectAltNames? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StringList Optional. A list of Subject Alternative Names (SANs) that the client verifies during a mutual TLS handshake with an server/endpoint for thisBackendService. When the server presents its X.509 certificate to the client, the client inspects the certificate'ssubjectAltName field. If the field contains one of the specified values, the communication continues. Otherwise, it fails. This additional check enables the client to verify that the server is authorized to run the requested service. Note that the contents of the server certificate's subjectAltName field are configured by the Public Key Infrastructure which provisions server identities. Only applies to a global BackendService withloadBalancingScheme set to INTERNAL_SELF_MANAGED. Only applies when BackendService has an attachedclientTlsPolicy with clientCertificate (mTLS mode).

