---Upcoming Maintenance notification information.
---@class gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpcomingMaintenance
---@field maintenanceOnShutdown? boolean Indicates whether the UpcomingMaintenance will be triggered on VM shutdown.
---@field maintenanceMethod? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpcomingMaintenanceMaintenanceMethodEnum|string Output only. Maintenance method for the upcoming maintenance.
---@field date? string [Output Only] The date when the maintenance will take place. This value is inRFC3339 text format. DEPRECATED: Use window_start_time instead.
---@field canReschedule? boolean Indicates if the maintenance can be customer triggered.
---@field windowStartTime? string The current start time of the maintenance window. This timestamp value is in RFC3339 text format.
---@field maintenanceReasons? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpcomingMaintenanceMaintenanceReasonsItemEnumList The reasons for the maintenance. Only valid for vms.
---@field windowEndTime? string The time by which the maintenance disruption will be completed. This timestamp value is in RFC3339 text format.
---@field latestWindowStartTime? string The latest time for the planned maintenance window to start. This timestamp value is in RFC3339 text format.
---@field startTimeWindow? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpcomingMaintenanceTimeWindow [Output Only] The start time window of the maintenance disruption. DEPRECATED: Use window_start_time instead. TimeWindow is a container for two strings that represent timestamps in "yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ssZ" text format.
---@field maintenanceStatus? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpcomingMaintenanceMaintenanceStatusEnum|string
---@field type? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpcomingMaintenanceTypeEnum|string Defines the type of maintenance.
---@field time? string [Output Only] The time when the maintenance will take place. This value is inRFC3339 text format. DEPRECATED: Use window_start_time instead.

