---@field lastStopTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Last stop timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field identity? string
---@field privateIpv6GoogleAccess? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstancePrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum|string The private IPv6 google access type for the VM. If not specified, use INHERIT_FROM_SUBNETWORK as default.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. [Output Only] Reserved for future use.
---@field partnerMetadata? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.StructuredEntriesMap Partner Metadata assigned to the instance. A map from a subdomain (namespace) to entries map.
---@field labelFingerprint? string A fingerprint for this request, which is essentially a hash of the label's contents and used for optimistic locking. The fingerprint is initially generated by Compute Engine and changes after every request to modify or update labels. You must always provide an up-to-date fingerprint hash in order to update or change labels. To see the latest fingerprint, make get() request to the instance.
---@field advancedMachineFeatures? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.AdvancedMachineFeatures Controls for advanced machine-related behavior features.
---@field shieldedInstanceConfig? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.ShieldedInstanceConfig
---@field status? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.InstanceStatusEnum|string Output only. [Output Only] The status of the instance. One of the following values: PROVISIONING, STAGING,RUNNING, STOPPING, SUSPENDING,SUSPENDED, REPAIRING, andTERMINATED. For more information about the status of the instance, see Instance life cycle.
---@field cpuPlatform? string Output only. [Output Only] The CPU platform used by this instance.
---@field lastSuspendedTimestamp? string Output only. [Output Only] Last suspended timestamp inRFC3339 text format.
---@field hostname? string Specifies the hostname of the instance. The specified hostname must be RFC1035 compliant. If hostname is not specified, the default hostname is [INSTANCE_NAME].c.[PROJECT_ID].internal when using the global DNS, and [INSTANCE_NAME].[ZONE].c.[PROJECT_ID].internal when using zonal DNS.
---@field id? string Output only. [Output Only] The unique identifier for the resource. This identifier is defined by the server.
---@field project string Project ID for this request.
---@field mostDisruptiveAllowedAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpdateInstancesMostDisruptiveAllowedActionEnum|string Specifies the most disruptive action that can be taken on the instance as part of the update. Compute Engine returns an error if the instance properties require a more disruptive action as part of the instance update. Valid options from lowest to highest are NO_EFFECT, REFRESH, and RESTART.
---@field minimalAction? gcp.unstable.compute_alpha.UpdateInstancesMinimalActionEnum|string Specifies the action to take when updating an instance even if the updated properties do not require it. If not specified, then Compute Engine acts based on the minimum action that the updated properties require.
